            <ArticleTitle>[Algesimetric measurement of the effect of cerebral electrotherapy on the pain threshold (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>567-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of cerebral electrotherapy (CET) on the pain threshold was investigated in 3 test persons, on 5 points of the neck of these persons. Altogether 1200 algesimetric measurements were performed. The statistical evaluation showed a significant tedency (p less than 0.01) towards an elevation of the pain threshold by CET.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
